which is if the government isn't hiding anything,

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.200
why is it hiding so much?

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:04.740
And he pointed out that in 1992, nearly 30
years after the assassination of the president,

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:11.060
80 percent of the government's records on
the subject were entirely classified.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.110
He put that in the trailer at the end of the
movie, and he said, If you're upset about

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:16.900
this, call your congressman.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:22.630
And so that resulted in a flood of mail to
Capitol Hill and Congress actually did the

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:23.630
right thing.

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:28.210
They said, we're going to release all these
records to quell all this speculation.

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:32.930
And so they passed a very strong law called
the JFK Records Act.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.540
It passed unanimously.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:39.470
Imagine that David unanimously something that
would never happen in today's political environment,

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:43.090
but pretty much everybody across the political
spectrum agreed.

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:45.870
All JFK records should be made public.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:52.400
And so the law created an independent board
to go and ask government agencies for their

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.400
records.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.430
The board reviewed them and released them
publicly.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:04.140
The agencies, the CIA, the FBI, the Pentagon,
they had the right to request the delay of

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:08.840
